ze: inherit; color: #00e;" target="_blank" title="马克·尼奎特 - 记者：政治 |彭博社"&gt;马克·尼奎特&lt;/a&gt;和&lt;a href="https://links.message.bloomberg.com/s/c/2DT81sGt_Q80FwmRERsWs6Zvk1ig5V_NdEecWY1AlRuVRysdaknFyf0Ztzdm8OszRoWOuKcO5m0oWa78CF1BMkrpNTMflKHI8cwGsXmA6mgV6vHuapmn3mXbulEvsdu1V8V8qdQu_2T0n4UGBYbMzxcuWM17gUMnW_e43pzUiWfSpRlqtD9Rirf3YXzOFim_sVWRRSYOGbXGS-SvZOzogmgrl2UIE8dj5LRFvAW1OzuC3epf-IlcHBsn5v027r1Gwf4xoDY2ykUOn55Oo3d-TkIS58IAJhfmjINsLgsA6s_JDBux1AKAafBZ3TBwGAwO3DtwPhXwG7bv8VXj3F2J-Z5VPGoqKRvV_4_oQ5C3R33uGE8u5IN3o-kFrSDo7qHV-xf_WjfM985efo1wQcRJ53Qpa4GNPjr8XzYKooOhz5g0s01hlu9b4wIrUByqaAm1s_7Tt2hlQ_Zl108Z1Gzuy_vJG-48Hrrd9IWsZvJePbpTnB69F8X3/uLX5SacnMrE2jjjlTIBe1pu9AQWiNR41/26" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-size: inherit; color: #00e;" target="_blank" title="劳伦·罗森塔尔 - 天气预报员 |彭博社"&gt;劳伦·罗森塔尔&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 24px; font-size: 16px;"&gt;美国人终于在汽油泵上得到了一些缓解，但食品价格的飙升才刚刚开始——正好赶上节日大餐。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 24px; font-size: 16px;"&gt;部分原因是能源成本上涨存在滞后性，这推高了农民使用的柴油、运输燃料和包装塑料的价格，从而流入超市过道。经济学家表示，继十月份的&lt;a href="https://links.message.bloomberg.com/a/sc/ihxgfaBGqE_0QNJaKvaMG1tWA9LS9ed7kT_HGEeOaVmZfeu9u3HYXMUWcu5jpe8f3q_QN2HPNDHTlGxUNg3udf1j73jllsh_994bkj3yoVnPXhjC6aiQw9aWa2tCp1eaN036DKIvuQt9g054qDDACMdN_z_hQdhz86wqOvNsGbzaHiYHme9dhOhiGmV0r8SbJ7op9C80yf0H1mIZrZ_PVH00vgOTjMU8RHu5-obtg7i0X_t9tDUn4_2Wyk7iw_14rv95Guktudi5UzUU10-TDcHBZwkaIYV9DjTQ_tGQu7c5hJfVxsd9MNVha05HZcmzMek7Fch0wTfe4gNgGy2FsMVmlPUqF8Zp45HtRjoNPzrKernz-v8nPDpKErvCItSqyxEi-wjTi_3CCB0xUSJrkzOU4qEdrA55_bzGeqL4Se1weunD7IHyNDrn7pRu3gxM5vMhTfuR50vSHcRMVNGqVfJf4mKCZLgNxzv5XSSW1Tzd9P9KuiRd8c_PWobOqA1VIHdxRkHZBArfQtS0Odt8gG0T9R8Y5ZC-aACUjDMRBAE0HvXP8G5jqiI/AuVzq_Y_vIup0pXlCh2-umnW9o2A5VRO/26" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-size: inherit; color: #00e;" target="_blank" title="美国核心CPI涨幅超过预期，支持美联储加息"&gt;大幅上涨&lt;/a&gt;之后，食品通胀将进一步恶化。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 24px; font-size: 16px;"&gt;生鲜产品通常首先受到冲击。根据&lt;a href="https://links.message.bloomberg.com/a/sc/2TievJLfqz0VFmpWYKDYBeCqU_